 decentralized trial-and-error. When regulators choose to halt deployment pipelines over unmeasured fears, they impose a heavy distributional toll on populations waiting for the very breakthroughs that automation accelerates. Who gave central planners the moral authority to withhold life-saving administrative relief from people who need it today?",
